<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!-- Styles taken from "Hallowen Monster Mash" ([KD] Killer_Diller).

       THE SOURCE HAS MOVED. These four styles used to read their textures straight out of the
       Steam mod, which worked only because that mod is inert in 1.6: it declares no
       LoadFolders.xml and keeps every def in a `1.2/` folder RimWorld never reads, while its
       textures sit at the root and load normally. It rendered, and nothing was copied - but it
       required a subscription to a mod dead since 2021.

       They now read from the 1.6 port instead, `nelim.halloweenmonstermash`, which ships all
       eleven decoration textures including these four. That is what LoadFolders.xml is
       conditioned on. The texPaths below are unchanged, because the port kept the author's
       texture layout.

       FOUR STYLES ONLY, and one category is enough since they target four different vanilla defs.

       THE OTHER SEVEN DECORATIONS - spider, ghosts, bats, skeleton, reaper, haunted tree, unlit
       pumpkin - are not styles and were never going to be: none has a vanilla twin. They are
       buildings in the port, where they belong. Do not add them here.

       ON THE TWO LIGHTS: in the source mod the lit jack-o-lantern and the candle are real
       buildings - Refuelable, a Glower of radius 10, a HeatPusher, even a meditation focus. As
       styles all of that is gone: the vanilla torch and brazier underneath keep their behaviour
       and only the appearance changes. That is the principle, and here it lands well - a torch
       lamp is already refuellable and already lights a room. The port deliberately does not
       rebuild those two as buildings, so the two mods never offer the same object twice. -->

  <StyleCategoryDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
    <defName>PAS_Halloween</defName>
    <label>halloween</label>
    <fixedIdeoOnly>false</fixedIdeoOnly>
    <thingDefStyles>
      <li>
        <thingDef>SculptureSmall</thingDef>
        <styleDef>PAS_Halloween_SculptureSmall</styleDef>
      </li>
      <li>
        <thingDef>TorchLamp</thingDef>
        <styleDef>PAS_Halloween_TorchLamp</styleDef>
      </li>
      <li>
        <thingDef>Campfire</thingDef>
        <styleDef>PAS_Halloween_Campfire</styleDef>
      </li>
      <li>
        <thingDef>Brazier</thingDef>
        <styleDef>PAS_Halloween_Brazier</styleDef>
      </li>
    </thingDefStyles>
  </StyleCategoryDef>

  <!-- La gargouille est litteralement une petite sculpture. -->
  <ThingStyleDef>
    <defName>PAS_Halloween_SculptureSmall</defName>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Decorations/Gargoyle/Gargoyle</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
  </ThingStyleDef>

  <!-- La citrouille allumee sur la torche : meme nature, une source de lumiere qu'on alimente. -->
  <ThingStyleDef>
    <defName>PAS_Halloween_TorchLamp</defName>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Decorations/JackolanternL/JackolanternL</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
  </ThingStyleDef>

  <!-- Le chaudron sur le feu de camp : on l'alimente, il chauffe, on y cuisine. -->
  <ThingStyleDef>
    <defName>PAS_Halloween_Campfire</defName>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Decorations/Cauldron/Cauldron</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
  </ThingStyleDef>

  <!-- La bougie sur le brasero. -->
  <ThingStyleDef>
    <defName>PAS_Halloween_Brazier</defName>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Decorations/Candle/Candle</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
  </ThingStyleDef>

</Defs>
